# Milestone: M3
# Covers: nonInterruptible mode prevents sleep/wait/barrier/semaphore blocking;
#         ',' separator in non-interruptible scope raises error; freeze interaction.
# defer-to: M6 (nonInterruptible keyword + M6 Semaphore/Barrier/Event types are hard dependencies)
#
# Reason:
#   'nonInterruptible' is a scheduler mode keyword that requires cooperation
#   between the strand scheduler and the runtime — deferred to M5.  The fixture
#   also uses 'import System.*', Tag.new()/freeze()/unfreeze() method dispatch (M4),
#   Semaphore/Barrier/Event types (M6), and ',' separator (M5 chk driver).
#
# Original urbiscript (activate at M5+ with full scheduler and stdlib):
# # import System.*;
# # { nonInterruptible; 1 };
# # [00000001] 1
# # { nonInterruptible; sleep(1s); 1 };
# # [00000002:error] !!! input.u:@.21-30: attempt to sleep in non-interruptible code
# # ... (see legacy/repos/aldebaran-urbi/tests/2.x/non-interruptible.chk)
